{{en-noun}}

# A [[grasp]] or grip.
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=7|passage=Old Applegate, in the stern, just set and looked at me, and Lord James, amidship, waved both arms and kept hollering for help. I took a couple of everlasting big strokes and managed to grab '''hold''' of the skiff's rail, close to the stern.}}
#: {{ux|en|Keep a firm '''hold''' on the handlebars.}}
# An act or instance of holding.
#: {{ux|en|Can I have a '''hold''' of the baby?}}
# A place where animals are held for safety
# An order that something is to be reserved or delayed, limiting or preventing how it can be dealt with.
#: {{ux|en|Senator X placed a '''hold''' on the bill, then went to the library and placed a '''hold''' on a book.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2008|author=R. Michael Gordon|title=The Space Shuttle Program: How NASA Lost Its Way|page=98
|passage=Because there were no “launch commit criteria” regarding surface booster temperatures that might cause a '''hold''' on the launch, the ice team did not report the temperatures to the launch controllers.}}
# Something reserved or [[kept]].
#: {{ux|en|We have a '''hold''' here for you.}}
# [[power|Power]] over someone or something.
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Dawn of the Messiah - Book 1|author=Christopher Clarke-Milton|year=2008|page=199|ISBN=1604777923|passage=The Judge accepts the payment, the law no longer has a '''hold''' on you, and therefore you are free to walk out of the court a free man or woman.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Inventing Peace: A Dialogue on Perception|author=Wim Wenders; Mary Zournazi|year=2013|page=107|ISBN=0857722700|passage=War has a '''hold''' on our cultural imaginations as an inevitable force, it is peace that has no benefactor.}}
# The [[ability]] to [[persist]].
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|XXVIII|45|This year I slept and woke with pain,<br>⁠I almost wish’d no more to wake,<br>⁠And that my '''hold''' on life would break<br>Before I heard those bells again: {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Rattlesnakes, Their Habits, Life Histories, and Influence|author=Laurence Monroe Klauber; Karen Harvey McClung|year=1982|page=48|ISBN=0520040392|passage=Despite their seemingly strong '''hold''' on life, as indicated by the persistence of movement in decapitation tests, rattlers are relatively frail creatures and are easily killed.}}
# The property of maintaining the [[shape]] of [[style]]d [[hair]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Zoe Diana Draelos|title=Hair Care: An Illustrated Dermatologic Handbook|page=221|passage=Sculpturing gels provide stiffer '''hold''' than styling gels, which provide better hold than mousses.}}
# {{senseid|en|position or grip to control an opponent}} {{lb|en|wrestling|self-defense}} A position or grip used to control the opponent.
#: {{ux|en|He got him in a tight '''hold''' and pinned him to the mat.}}
# {{lb|en|exercise}} An exercise involving holding a position for a set time
# {{lb|en|[[gambling]]}} The percentage the house wins on a gamble, the house or bookmaker's hold.
#* {{quote-web|1=en|year=2002|author="Reality"|title=The Scorecard For Bookmakers|url=http://www.majorwager.com/forums/mess-hall/104970-scorecard-bookmakers-reality.html#post867194|accessdate=2013-12-18|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20150427112952/http://www.majorwager.com/forums/mess-hall/104970-scorecard-bookmakers-reality.html#post867194|archivedate=27 April 2015}}
#: {{ux|en|The House '''Hold''' on the game is 10,000, this is the amount of decision or risk the house wishes to assume.}}
# {{lb|en|[[gambling]]}} The wager amount, the total '''hold'''.
#* {{quote-web|1=en|year=2012|author=Sarah Fortnum|title=Melbourne Cup 2012 From The Bookie’s Perspective|url=http://www.races.com.au/2012/11/06/melbourne-cup-2012-from-the-bookies-perspective/|accessdate=2013-12-18|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20121112220603/http://www.races.com.au/2012/11/06/melbourne-cup-2012-from-the-bookies-perspective/|archivedate=12 November 2012}}
#: ''As of Monday night the total Melbourne Cup '''hold''' was $848,015''
# {{lb|en|tennis}} An instance of [[hold#Verb|holding]] one's service game, as opposed to being [[break#Verb|broken]].
# The part of an object one is intended to grasp, or anything one can use for grasping with hands or feet.
#* {{RQ:Falkner Moonfleet|year=1934|passage=So I felt my way down the passage back to the vault, and recked not of the darkness, nor of Blackbeard and his crew, if only I could lay my lips to liquor. Thus I groped about the barrels till near the top of the stack my hand struck on the spile of a keg, and drawing it, I got my mouth to the '''hold'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Rock Climbing Basics|author=Turlough Johnston; Madeleine Halldén|year=1995|page=86|ISBN=0811724204|passage=The beginner will instinctively try to stick his toe straight in in a foot '''hold''', which is very tiring on the calf muscles.}}
# A [[fruit machine]] feature allowing one or more of the [[reel]]s to remain fixed while the others [[spin]].
# {{lb|en|video games|dated}} A [[pause]] facility.
#* '''1983''', New Generation Software, ''Knot in 3D'' (video game instruction leaflet)
#*: A '''hold''' facility is available; H holds, and S restarts.
#* '''1987'''?, Imagine Software, ''Legend of Kage'' (video game instruction leaflet)
#*: SCREEN 5 — Perhaps the toughest — going like the clappers sometimes works but generally you'll have to be smarter than that. If things get a little too hectic and you don't even have time to reach the '''HOLD''' key, try taking a short rest below the top of the stairs.
# The [[queueing]] system on telephones and similar communication systems which maintains a connection when all lines are busy.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=Daniel Jackson; Paul Fulberg|title=Sonic Branding: An Essential Guide to the Art and Science of Sonic Branding|publisher=Palgrave Macmillan|isbn=9780230503267|page=6
|passage=Given that there is an average on-hold time of more than five minutes while enquiries are being dealt with, the telephone '''hold''' system provided the best opportunity.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=Lorraine Grubbs-West|title=Lessons in Loyalty: How Southwest Airlines Does it : an Insider's View|publisher=CornerStone Leadership Inst|isbn=9780976252856|page=56
|passage=Even the "on-hold" messages on Southwest&#39;s telephone system are humorous, ensuring anyone inconvenienced by the '''hold''' is entertained.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Tanner Ezell|title=Cisco Unified Communications Manager 8: Expert Administration Cookbook|publisher=Packt Publishing Ltd|isbn=9781849684330
|passage=Note. After the device downloads its new configuration file, we can test placing a call on '''hold''' and the generic '''hold''' music will be heard.}}
# {{lb|en|baseball}} A [[statistic]] awarded to a [[relief pitcher]] who is not still pitching at the end of the game and who records at least one [[out]] and maintains a lead for his team.
# {{lb|en|aviation}} A region of [[airspace]] reserved for aircraft being kept in a [[holding pattern]].

